\subsection{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}

All closed-loop evaluations use the LIBERO simulation benchmark. Although prior work has shown LIBERO policies transfer to real hardware, pruning-induced degradation patterns may differ under real-world perception noise; we provide no sim-to-real evidence. The six architectures differ in backbone, encoder, and scale beyond the connector, preventing causal isolation of the connector effect. While CV is measured across all six architectures, the correlation between CV and closed-loop pruning tolerance relies on four models, too few to establish a general law. Our pruning methods are limited to L2 norm selection and random subsampling; attention-based scoring~\cite{chen2024fastv} may yield different robustness profiles. VTR is validated on SmolVLA only; whether learned re-encoding generalizes to other entangling connectors is untested. Most conditions use a single seed (seed 42); seven-condition cross-seed validation shows $\Delta \leq 5.8$\,pp (Appendix~\ref{app:pi05_multiseed},~\ref{app:openvla_multiseed}). Pruning is applied post-connector; pre-connector or KV-cache-level compression~\cite{xu2025vlacache} may interact differently with connector coupling. Extended discussion is in Appendix~\ref{app:discussion}.

